Mutant m5: emit every wasm print twice (the wasm-only divergence).

Seeded into the STRUCTURAL emitter's print lowering (crates/almide-wasm
lower_print, both the interpolation branch — the flush call issued twice —
and the String-block branch — the argument lowered and printed twice):
the default wasm leg since 0.60 (#1696), and the leg the conformance
runner builds every corpus program on (48/48 via `almide build --target
wasm` with no ALMIDE_WASM_INCUMBENT). The previous form of this mutant
seeded the same bug into the incumbent renderer (almide-mir
render_wasm_c.rs, RtFn::PrintStr) and SURVIVED seven nights once the
route flipped: the runner never executed that code, so nothing could
kill it (#1845). The incumbent carries no mutant now. A mutant on a leg
the corpus does not build on is not evidence, it is noise.

